# SCRATCH BUILDS OF AN OLDER REVISION, written here and deleted again.
#
# Several tools measure a change against the build before it — devtools/harness
# `openDrive({rev})` writes `client/__rev-main.ts`, and any test that needs a
# probe the old build lacks grafts its own copy beside it (dock-sky, road-hole).
# They live INSIDE client/ on purpose: main.ts imports ./menu and ./overlays by
# relative path and three from the repo's node_modules, so a copy bundled out of
# a temp directory resolves none of them.
#
# Each of them is a ~2MB stale duplicate of main.ts. They are removed in a
# `finally`, and that removal is the real guard — `cell-sync push` sends every
# file in the cell and does not read this file, so one left behind by a crashed
# run gets DEPLOYED as cell source. This keeps `git status` honest so the stray
# is visible while it exists, rather than committed by a tidy-up.
client/__rev-main.ts
client/__*-rev.ts
